==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|tīwa-|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|dhyeu-|god|lang=ang}}.

Proto-Germanic cognate with Old Norse {{term|Tyr|Týr|lang=non}}, Old High German [[Zio|Zīo]], Gothic [[𐍄𐌴𐌶]].

PIE cognate with Ancient Greek {{term|Ζευς|lang=grc}}, Latin {{term|lovis|lang=la}}, Hittite {{term|sc=Xsux|𒅆𒍑|tr=sius|lang=hit}}, {{proto|Slavic|divъ|title=Common Slavic|lang=}} (Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrl|дивъ|tr=divŭ|lang=cu}}), Sanskrit {{term|द्यु |tr=dyú|sc=Deva|lang=sa}}.

